from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/'manuscript'
p=root/'main.tex';s=p.read_text()
s=s.replace(' The broader architecture supports richer logical views and learned proposal interfaces. The measured configuration uses propositional checking, signed capabilities, and durable consumption.','')
a=s.index('Complete mediation requires');b=s.index('\\section{From source documents',a)
s=s[:a]+r'''Complete mediation requires each protected access to pass an authorization check \citep{saltzer1975protection}. Security automata, inlined monitors, and edit automata characterize runtime-enforceable policies \citep{schneider2000enforceable,erlingsson2000irm,ligatti2005edit,hamlen2006enforcement}. AgentSpec supplies runtime triggers and rules \citep{wang2025agentspec}; Progent checks symbolic tool privileges and policy updates \citep{shi2025progent}; CaMeL uses capabilities to isolate agent data flow \citep{debenedetti2025camel}. We connect this enforcement boundary to source-derived constraints and exact invocation context.

\paragraph{Executable law and checked evidence.}
Formalizing a statute entails an interpretation of the source \citep{sergot1986bna,prakken2015lawlogic,benzmueller2020logikey}. Catala makes legal specifications executable \citep{catala}; Mlang compiles the French tax code \citep{merigoux2021tax}. Proof-carrying code and authentication place checked evidence before execution or authorization \citep{necula1997pcc,appel1999pca}, while translation validation and CompCert explicitly connect translation to verification \citep{pnueli1998translation,leroy2009compcert}. Our design similarly distinguishes source fidelity, translation, and checker output; its evaluated propositional evidence is narrower than a kernel-checked theorem.

\paragraph{Capabilities and policy languages.}
Object capabilities, attenuating caveats, relation-based authorization, and policy languages restrict authority in complementary ways \citep{miller2006robust,birgisson2014macaroons,pang2019zanzibar,cutler2024cedar}. UCAN supplies signed delegated capabilities \citep{ucan}. Both our lightweight baseline and full mechanism verify capabilities; the latter additionally binds current context and durable use state. This application check complements MCP transport authorization \citep{mcp-auth}.

\paragraph{Coding and tool-agent evaluation.}
Code-generation and issue-resolution benchmarks emphasize functional correctness \citep{chen2021codex,jimenez2024swebench}. Verified generation, theorem proving, and autoformalization connect programs or specifications to formal checks \citep{sun2024clover,yang2023leandojo,wu2022autoformalization}. AgentDojo, ToolEmu, InjecAgent, $\tau$-bench, and AgentHarm examine attacks, risky actions, policy following, and harmful tool use \citep{debenedetti2024agentdojo,ruan2024toolemu,zhan2024injecagent,yao2024taubench,andriushchenko2025agentharm}. Our comparison measures forbidden effects alongside allowed work within one implementation; these external systems were not executed as baselines.

'''+s[b:]
s=s.replace('Original documents remain separate from normalized provisions, with jurisdiction, publication status, effective interval, and retrieval provenance intact.', 'Original documents remain separate from normalized provisions, preserving recorded jurisdiction, publication status, effective interval when known, and retrieval provenance.')
s=s.replace('The three IRs share canonical identity, provenance, schema, and result contracts while retaining different semantics. Original sources and derived views remain independently addressable. Sparse, vector, and graph retrieval nominate evidence; applicability and exact identity determine whether it may enter a decision. A citation edge is not a logical implication, and a retrieved neighbor is not controlling authority. Appendix~\\ref{app:corpus} records source revisions and sampling context for the 30 evaluated families.', 'The IRs share identity, provenance, schema, and result contracts while retaining different semantics. Sources and derived views remain independently addressable. Retrieval nominates evidence; applicability determines whether it may enter a decision. Citation edges do not establish logical implications. Appendix~\\ref{app:corpus} records source revisions and sampling context.')
p.write_text(s)
p=root/'design.tex';s=p.read_text().replace('an unused grant','available permitted use')
s=s.replace('Changes to source, policy, revocation, or environment roots trigger renewed checking of affected obligations.', 'Reuse requires renewed checking after relevant source, policy, revocation, or environment roots change.')
s=s.replace('Normalization, premise selection, tactic selection, and replanning can be supplied by learned components through proposal interfaces. Acceptance follows the declared checking contract. A similarity score cannot establish entailment, and a successful paraphrase cannot repair a missing obligation. Rejection witnesses identify affected actions and missing evidence so a proposing agent can revise the relevant part of a plan. No trained normalizer, encoder, or model-guided replanning was used in the scored experiment.', 'Learned components can propose normalizations, premises, tactics, or revised plans. Acceptance follows the checking contract: similarity cannot establish entailment or repair a missing obligation. Rejection witnesses identify affected actions and missing evidence for local revision. Trained normalization, encoding, and replanning were not evaluated.')
p.write_text(s)
p=root/'runtime.tex';s=p.read_text()
s=s.replace('Legal applicability checks jurisdiction, authority, time, definitions, and exceptions; security applicability checks the principal, asset, channel, action, effect, and environment.', 'In the broader design, legal applicability jobs bind jurisdiction, authority, time, definitions, and exceptions; security jobs bind the principal, asset, channel, action, effect, and environment.')
s=s.replace('In explicit \\texttt{ENFORCE}, permitted use is consumed', 'In the evaluated \\texttt{ENFORCE} configuration, permitted use is consumed')
s=s.replace('Consider a procedure requesting a JSON export. Its Intent IR records the selected data, destination, prerequisites, and expected effect. Applicable source constraints enter the decision with their required evidence. Changing the recipient invalidates the invocation binding, while replaying a consumed request fails the use-state check. An independent filesystem journal records whether the handler actually mutated the sandbox and whether allowed work succeeded. An authorization response alone does not count as successful execution. Appendix~\\ref{app:trace} exposes a separate diagnostic replay with intermediate checks; it adds no scored observations.', 'For a JSON export, Intent IR records the data, destination, prerequisites, and expected effect. Changing the recipient invalidates the invocation binding; replay fails the use-state check. An independent filesystem journal measures mutations and allowed work, separately from the authorization response. Appendix~\\ref{app:trace} exposes intermediate checks in a diagnostic replay that adds no scored observations.')
p.write_text(s)
p=root/'extensions.tex';p.write_text(r'''\section{Extensions toward closed-loop agents}
\label{sec:extensions}

A closed-loop study would ask whether an agent can use rejection witnesses to repair a plan, obtain missing evidence, and complete useful work. A failed applicability check should identify the affected source and obligation. The fixed-action results establish neither the semantic quality of that feedback nor a model's ability to act on it.

A task-specific \emph{ContextPack} would carry selected source and proof dependencies, with local aliases mapped to original content identities, instead of whole collections. Semantic minification must preserve required obligations, source maps, unsupported facets, and current-root dependencies. Retrieval relevance cannot certify that an omitted constraint is irrelevant. Evaluation should measure context size, token use, compilation and checking overhead, invalidation, and authorized task utility. No compressor or token-saving result is reported here.

Further directions include revision-aware program states, exact or abstract transitions, learned next-action and inverse-trace proposals, and semantics-preserving refactoring with parallel validation and checked test reuse. Their evaluation must account for both preservation of the required guarantees and checking cost.
''')
p=root/'checklist.tex';s=p.read_text().replace('The paper presents an empirical systems study and makes no theoretical claims requiring a proof. The evaluated QF\\_BOOL route supplies satisfiability evidence.', 'The paper presents an empirical systems study. Equation~\\ref{eq:admission} summarizes the design contract; no soundness theorem is claimed. The evaluated QF\\_BOOL route supplies satisfiability evidence.')
p.write_text(s)
